WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:10.600 line:91%,end align:center size:90%
A miner fills in a block header and tries a nonce.

2
00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:15.500 line:91%,end align:center size:90%
Each attempt runs 100,000 sequential rounds over a 32 × 32 integer problem,
reading a 4 GB dataset and a 4 GB scratchpad that depend on the running state.

3
00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:20.600 line:91%,end align:center size:90%
A stability check closes the attempt with a 32-byte commitment.
It wins only if it is below the target set by cASERT.

4
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:27.600 line:91%,end align:center size:90%
Transactions are gathered into a block.
A Merkle root commits to all of them.

5
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.200 line:91%,end align:center size:90%
Since block #7,100 every block carries the miner’s public key
and a Schnorr (BIP-340) signature — SbPoW.

6
00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:38.200 line:91%,end align:center size:90%
Every node recomputes the proof of work and the difficulty
and checks every rule before it accepts the block.

7
00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:44.000 line:91%,end align:center size:90%
A wallet signs a transaction in the browser.
The private key never leaves the device.

8
00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.400 line:91%,end align:center size:90%
Nodes relay it to their peers.
It waits in each node’s mempool.

9
00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:51.800 line:91%,end align:center size:90%
A miner includes it in the next block.

10
00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:57.800 line:91%,end align:center size:90%
Since block #25,000 every block pays 50 % to its miner
and 50 % to the DTD — subsidy and fees alike.

11
00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:02.600 line:91%,end align:center size:90%
The DTD draws one winner per block, uniformly,
among addresses that produced a signed block in the last 288 blocks.

12
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:07.200 line:91%,end align:center size:90%
Cooldown and anti-dominance rules apply.
An unpaid share rolls over.

13
00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:12.800 line:91%,end align:center size:90%
Former vault and pool balances form a frozen consensus reserve.
Only the Jackpot rule can spend it.

14
00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:16.800 line:91%,end align:center size:90%
Every 288 blocks: base 100 SOST, capped at 500, with rollover.

15
00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:20.800 line:91%,end align:center size:90%
Winners need ≥ 3 PoW blocks in the last 2,016, an active NODE_BIND and heartbeats.
Weight grows with PoW blocks, not with the number of nodes.

16
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.400 line:91%,end align:center size:90%
V16 is the consensus in force today.

17
00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:30.400 line:91%,end align:center size:90%
V17 proposes 80 % miner · 15 % DTD · 5 % to a Jackpot accumulator,
new winner seeds, full re-execution of proofs and native multisig.

18
00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:34.300 line:91%,end align:center size:90%
It is not active and no release has been published.
It would activate only if nodes and miners adopt a release before #40,000.

19
00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:39.800 line:91%,end align:center size:90%
Planned: record an asset’s fingerprint on chain
and have it verified by a quorum of custodians.

20
00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:44.800 line:91%,end align:center size:90%
On mainnet the asset layer is switched off (fail-closed).
Public issuance stays disabled.

21
00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:49.800 line:91%,end align:center size:90%
The gate can only open or restrict new issuance —
it can never move, freeze or confiscate SOST or existing assets.

22
00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:55.400 line:91%,end align:center size:90%
Design: an ERC-20 at 1 SOST = 1 wSOST, from a fixed inventory
released only against verified SOST deposits.

23
00:01:55.800 --> 00:02:00.400 line:91%,end align:center size:90%
The current design exists only in a local laboratory: no wSOST contract on Ethereum, no official address.
An earlier, different prototype was tested on the Sepolia testnet and has been retired.

24
00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:05.300 line:91%,end align:center size:90%
Before any value: new SOST consensus rules, decentralised block production,
an independent external audit and legal review.
